---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { guides } from '../../lib/guides';

const guideCards = [
  { href: '/oopbuy-spreadsheet/', title: 'How to use an Oopbuy spreadsheet', group: 'Getting started', description: 'The complete route from category discovery to live listing, QC and shipping.' },
  { href: '/guides/oopbuy-spreadsheet-categories/', title: 'Oopbuy spreadsheet categories', group: 'Getting started', description: 'Why category-first research produces a better shortlist than a mixed mega-list.' },
  { href: '/guides/oopbuy-qc-photos/', title: 'Oopbuy QC photos', group: 'QC & checks', description: 'What warehouse photos show, how to read the count, and what to check before shipping.' },
  { href: '/guides/oopbuy-size-guide/', title: 'How to check product sizes', group: 'QC & checks', description: 'Use measurements from a similar item you own instead of relying on size labels.' },
  { href: '/guides/oopbuy-shipping-guide/', title: 'Oopbuy shipping guide', group: 'Shipping', description: 'Prepare a parcel carefully and verify the live shipping option at checkout.' },
  ...Object.entries(guides).map(([slug, guide]) => ({ href: `/guides/${slug}/`, title: guide.title, group: guide.group, description: guide.description }))
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Oopbuy Guides: QC, Categories, Size & Shipping | OopbuyTop" description="Independent Oopbuy spreadsheet guides for category research, live listing checks, warehouse QC photos, sizing and shipping decisions.">
 <section class="guides-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Independent buyer resource</p><h1>Oopbuy Spreadsheet Guides</h1><p>Use the right guide at the right point: narrow a category, compare current details, review warehouse QC, then plan a parcel.</p></section>
 <section class="guides-explainer"><div><p class="eyebrow">Use the guide like a map</p><h2>Research first. Decide with the live details.</h2></div><div><p>A spreadsheet is useful for discovery, but it cannot replace current stock, options, measurements, shipping availability or support terms. Each guide below answers one specific decision so you can move from a short list to a clear next step without treating an old card as a checkout page.</p><a class="text-link" href="/oopbuy-spreadsheet/">Read the complete spreadsheet workflow →</a></div></section>
 <section class="guide-method"><p class="eyebrow">The four-part method</p><h2>Build a short list that survives real checks.</h2><div class="guide-method-grid"><article><b>01</b><h3>Choose one category</h3><p>Compare similar products in one lane instead of scrolling a mixed list of unrelated items.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h3>Verify the live listing</h3><p>Confirm the exact variant, current price, measurements and seller images before you act.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h3>Review warehouse QC</h3><p>Use reference photos to compare the received item with the option you selected.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h3>Check shipping live</h3><p>Read the current destination-specific service and restrictions at checkout, not an old quote.</p></article></div></section>
 <section class="guides-hub">{['Getting started', 'QC & checks', 'Shipping'].map((group) => <div class="guide-group"><div class="guide-group-head"><p class="eyebrow">{group}</p><h2>{group === 'Getting started' ? 'Find and compare with context' : group === 'QC & checks' ? 'Verify the item before the parcel' : 'Finish with current shipping details'}</h2></div><div class="guide-list">{guideCards.filter((guide) => guide.group === group).map((guide) => <a class="guide-card" href={guide.href}><span class="guide-card-number">0{guideCards.indexOf(guide) + 1}</span><h3>{guide.title}</h3><p>{guide.description}</p><b>Read guide →</b></a>)}</div></div>)}</section>
 <section class="guides-explainer guides-intent"><div><p class="eyebrow">Which guide should I open?</p><h2>Start from the question you actually have.</h2></div><div><p><strong>Looking for a product?</strong> Start with categories. <strong>Choosing between similar listings?</strong> Read price research and the product comparison guide. <strong>Unsure about a label or fit?</strong> Use the size guide before an item is ordered. <strong>Item at a warehouse?</strong> Open the QC guide. <strong>Ready to make a parcel?</strong> Read the shipping guide.</p><p>That sequence also keeps the site’s information honest: research pages help you compare, while live destination pages remain the source for checkout decisions.</p></div></section>
 <section class="guide-faq"><p class="eyebrow">Before you start</p><h2>Guide FAQ</h2><details><summary>Is this an official Oopbuy service?</summary><p>No. OopbuyTop is an independent research resource. Use official services for accounts, payment, orders and support.</p></details><details><summary>Can a spreadsheet confirm an item is available?</summary><p>No. It is a discovery tool. Confirm availability, options and price on the current live listing.</p></details><details><summary>Do QC photos guarantee product quality?</summary><p>No. They are a useful warehouse reference, not a guarantee. Compare them with the selected listing and decide before shipment.</p></details></section>
</BaseLayout>
